      "description": "Black Hills Colorado IPP, LLC is the manager-level independent-power investment within the broader Pueblo Airport Generating Station in Pueblo County, Colorado. The full site totals 440 MW, but the IPP company owns the 200 MW combined-cycle facility that entered service in 2012; the other 240 MW is utility-owned and is not part of Argo's investment. Black Hills Electric Generation retains a 50.1% controlling interest and the operating role, while Argo Infrastructure Partners manages the AIA Energy North America structure whose AIA Colchis vehicle holds the remaining 49.9%. AIA signed for the interest on February 12, 2016 and closed on April 14, 2016. The IPP sells capacity and energy to Black Hills Colorado Electric under a contract running through December 31, 2031. Black Hills' August 2026 filing continued to report the IPP noncontrolling interest, and no Argo/AIA exit or signed pending IPP ownership transfer was identified through August 16, 2026.",
